Hardware Layer — Encoders

The firmware exclusively supports incremental encoders outputting A/B impulses. The Z index is not used, so whether or not the encoder has it is irrelevant. 
FFbeast

For optimal performance with a hoverboard motor with no reduction, 1000 CPR or higher is recommended directly on the motor shaft. 
FFbeast

Three encoder tiers exist: the budget option is the MT6701 magnetic encoder at 4096 CPR — what the reference build uses. Mid-tier is the MT6825 at 16384 CPR. Top tier is the CUI AMT-10E2 or AMT-10E3 at 20480 CPR — the preferred option for the project creator's own builds. 
FFbeast + 2

Important warning: the TLE5012B encoder is explicitly not recommended — it has a programmed dead zone that introduces artificial backlash when changing direction, directly degrading force feedback feel. 
FFbeast

Also critical: magnetic encoders are extremely sensitive to magnet placement — off-axis placement causes non-linearity in calculated forces. If precision mounting isn't achievable, switch encoder type. 
FFbeast

Reference Build BOM

The reference build uses: MKS XDrive single axis ($45-50), hoverboard motor ($10-30), MT6701 encoder ($2-3), six SK16 pillow blocks ($10-15), a 16mm shaft at 150mm ($3-5), 3D printed enclosure ($10-30), breakout PCB ($2-3), and quick release hub ($10-15). Total for the base only: $85-160 USD. 
FFbeast

The breakout PCB is publicly available on EasyEDA — JLCPCB will produce five of them for about $2. 
FFbeast

PSU

You can use any PSU from 12V up to the rated voltage of your ODrive variant. For medium forces a 240-250W supply is sufficient — a Dell laptop PSU at 19.5V/12.3A is a popular clean option. For absolute maximum torque from the motor, 300W+ per motor is needed, requiring a modular open-frame PSU like a MeanWell or ATX unit. 
github

There's also a clever parallel PSU solution: the project creator designed a PCB for paralleling two identical Dell laptop PSUs, giving full enclosed-case power without open terminals — the only requirement is both PSUs must be identical in voltage and power rating. 
github

ODrive Configuration for Hoverboard Motors

Hoverboard hub motors are high resistance and high inductance compared to hobby aircraft motors. The calibration requires: resistance_calib_max_voltage = 4, requested_current_range = 25, current_control_bandwidth = 100, and torque_constant = 8.27 / measured KV. Typical KV for a hoverboard motor is around 16 if unmeasured. 
