Clutch — M18 drills have an adjustable clutch. You'd need to lock it to maximum or disable it entirely, otherwise it'll slip under FFB load. Some drills have a drill mode that bypasses the clutch — use that.

Bearing loads — the gearbox output bearing is designed for axial chuck loads, not the radial loads a belt pulley puts on it. Worth adding an external pillow block bearing on the output shaft to take that load off the drill's internal bearing.

