This is actually a really interesting find. The stock hoverboard mainboard can be repurposed with custom firmware.

The stock hoverboard mainboard runs an STM32F103RCT6 (or GD32F103RCT6) and supports UART, PWM, PPM and iBUS input through the original sideboard cable connectors. The hoverboard-firmware-hack-FOC project replaces the stock firmware with proper FOC control including voltage mode, speed mode, and torque mode. 
