The real problem: The VESC needs to report encoder position back to OpenFFBoard via CAN for FOC torque control to work properly. Without position feedback the VESC can't do closed loop torque mode — it has no idea where the motor is sitting, meaning FFB forces will be wrong or cause runaway.

