Sideload com.ik.simwheel_5.2.2_patched_arm64-only.apk (or install the XAPK with an XAPK installer).
Open the app and connect to the PC Receiver normally — the original IP/discovery UI is unchanged. Allow the phone on the receiver as usual.
Pair your Bluetooth controller to the phone. As soon as you press anything on it, the bridge will fire UDP packets from the phone's IP, so the receiver sees them as coming from the same allowed phone.
L2/R2 will arrive at the receiver as throttle/brake analog (0.0–1.0). Face buttons arrive as vJoy buttons 1–24, D-pad as 25–28. Combine with my prior receiver patch (receiver_repo_patched_full_preserve_features.zip) so the receiver handles these partial packets (no steering field) without crashing.
